  b: repo-internal-source
split: genuinely-split
draft_status: axis-only
leverage: 2
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(2) x split_weight(1) x authored_conflict_bonus(1)"

question: >
  On source admissibility — whether only material already inside the tree may be
  cited as backing, or outside artifacts and services count — the records assert
  both outside source admitted (1 judgments, 0 authored) and repo internal
  source (1 judgments, 0 authored). Which should be the stated rule, and where
  is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

